;; gen.laws, the GFI's laws as test.check properties: a module of gen.clj
;; outside its core (DESIGN.md §9, "The 1.0's shape"). A dependent takes it
;; as a git dependency on gen.clj's repository with :deps/root "ext/laws",
;; at the commit of the gen.clj it uses:
;;
;;   gen.clj/laws {:git/url "…gen.clj" :git/sha "…" :deps/root "ext/laws"}
;;
;; It brings gen.clj from the same checkout. A dependent that names gen.clj
;; as gen.clj/gen.clj itself, at the top of its deps, keeps its own: tools.deps
;; takes a top-level dependency over a transitive one. In gen.clj's own
;; repository the :laws and :test aliases put ext/laws/src on the classpath.
{:paths ["src"]
 :deps {org.clojure/test.check {:mvn/version "1.1.3"}
        gen.clj/gen.clj {:local/root "../.."}}}
